# SCRIPT ERROR lines `tools/quiet.sh` will not fail a run for. Card #63.
#
# THIS FILE IS A DEBT LEDGER AND NOT A CONFIGURATION. Every row is a director
# that is printing a real GDScript error and getting away with it, held open
# only until the card in column three closes. An exempt error is still printed
# and still counted; it just does not set exit 65. Nothing here is a decision
# that the error is acceptable.
#
# Three tab-separated columns, `#` starts a comment:
#
#   <director file name>  <substring of the message>  <card>
#
# The director is matched on the BASENAME of `--director=`, so an exemption can
# never leak to another director. The message is matched as a plain substring of
# the text after `SCRIPT ERROR: `, so it can never leak to another failure in the
# same file either -- which is the whole rule the card set: per-director AND
# per-message, never a blanket "ignore stderr". There is deliberately no switch
# that turns the gate off wholesale; a run you cannot make clean is a card, and
# adding the row here is how you file it.
#
# Taken 2026-08-11 from a sweep of all 136 directors on `main` at 661582b. See
# CLAUDE.md §2. Cards #70 and #71 removed the three discovered exemptions; the
# ledger is currently empty.
